description:
repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/fossil-rank-report.ts can never detect a fossil, because line 17 reads `const fileLineCounts = pointer.fileLineCounts ?? {};` and no caller ever supplies `fileLineCounts` — the only dispatch site passes the request pointer straight through — so the loop at line 20 iterates an empty object. Right now development-vessel holds src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts at 3133 lines and src/resolvers/vessel-mitosis-cutover.ts at 2780 lines, both over the ceiling of 2000, and resolving {"type":"fossilRankReport"} with no arguments returns {"fossils":[],"ceiling":2000}.

Do not write this from a description. Apply the two literal edits below exactly as given.

EDIT 1 — replace this exact line, which occurs once at line 17:

  const fileLineCounts = pointer.fileLineCounts ?? {};

with this exact line:

  const fileLineCounts = pointer.fileLineCounts ?? (await collectLineCounts());

EDIT 2 — replace this exact line, which occurs once at line 15:

export async function resolveFossilRankReport(pointer: FossilRankReportPointer): Promise<FossilRankReportResult> {

with this exact block (the helper first, then the unchanged function signature):

async function collectLineCounts(): Promise<Record<string, number>> {
  const root = process.env["VESSEL_SRC_ROOT"] ?? "src";
  const skip = new Set(["node_modules", "dist", ".git", "test"]);
  const counts: Record<string, number> = {};
  const walk = async (dir: string): Promise<void> => {
    const entries = await readdir(dir, { withFileTypes: true });
    for (const entry of entries) {
      if (skip.has(entry.name)) continue;
      const full = join(dir, entry.name);
      if (entry.isDirectory()) {
        await walk(full);
      } else if (entry.isFile() && entry.name.endsWith(".ts")) {
        const text = await readFile(full, "utf8");
        counts[relative(root, full)] = text.split("\n").length;
      }
    }
  };
  try {
    await walk(root);
  } catch {
    return {};
  }
  return counts;
}

export async function resolveFossilRankReport(pointer: FossilRankReportPointer): Promise<FossilRankReportResult> {

The imports this helper needs are ALREADY PRESENT at lines 7 and 8 (`readdir`, `readFile` from node:fs/promises and `join`, `relative` from node:path). Do not add imports; do not move or duplicate them.

Change nothing else. Leave the weight formula, the `lines > ceiling` test, the sort, the ceiling default of 2000, and the returned shape exactly as they are.

Note on intent, so it is not mistaken for an unfixed condition: when a caller DOES pass `fileLineCounts`, that value must still win and the filesystem must not be touched. That override is deliberate and required — existing callers and tests depend on it. The gap is that there is no fallback when nothing is supplied, and this patch adds exactly that fallback.

Observable result: resolving {"type":"fossilRankReport"} with no arguments must return a non-empty `fossils` array including gap-to-feature.ts and vessel-mitosis-cutover.ts, instead of the empty array it returns today.

